<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Close of play scores on the first</p>
<p>day of four-day English County Championship cricket matches on</p>
<p>Wednesday:</p>
<p>At Southampton: Lancashire 423-5 (A.Flintoff 117,</p>
<p>M.Watkinson 102 not out, G.Lloyd 90, N.Wood 82) v Hampshire.</p>
<p>At Leicester: Nottinghamshire 296-9 (M.Dowman 125 not out) v</p>
<p>Leicestershire.</p>
<p>At Chelmsford: Worcestershire 328-6 (K.Spiring 119 not out,</p>
<p>V.Solanki 60) v Essex.</p>
<p>At Northampton: Surrey 386-4 (D.Bicnkell 162, A.Hollioake</p>
<p>81, A.Brown 63 not out) v Surrey.</p>
<p>At Chesterfield: Derbyshire 379-4 (A.Rollins 148, M.May 116)</p>
<p>v Glamorgan.</p>
<p>At Cheltenham: Durham 86 (M.Alleyne 5-14). Gloucestershire</p>
<p>253-5 (M.Alleyne 77 not out M.Windows 75, S.Young 52; S.Brown</p>
<p>4-71).</p>
<p>At Lord's: Kent 208 (A.Wells 63). Middlesex 103-9 (M.McCague</p>
<p>6-49).</p>
</text>
